  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The operating backdrop is favorable, led by strong momentum in experiential services and a meaningful improvement in retailer-services profitability. External demand signals are supportive: a company-sponsored survey indicates private brands now drive store choice for the majority of shoppers, reinforcing demand for the firm’s merchandising, marketing, and CPG solutions. The macro environment appears benign, with management reaffirming its outlook and seeing no material softening in client activity.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is actively reshaping the operating model—deploying a centralized labor structure that is lifting execution, productivity, and margins. The team is simultaneously strengthening the balance sheet by reducing debt, which has lowered leverage. Coupled with a reaffirmed full-year guidance, these moves, along with post-split capital actions, signal disciplined capital allocation and are rebuilding market confidence in execution.",
